DECISION
AR-H111 is POSITIVE WITH A RAW-CORRELATION AUTHORITY FAILURE.

Supported synthetically:

- historical predictive payoff can credential a purely contextual proxy;
- context/provenance conditioning rejects that spurious authority;
- unique direct alarm value survives correlation shift;
- direct alarm quality can later degrade;
- recency-aware credentialing revokes stale fast authority;
- a high-specificity alternative can inherit fast authority;
- emergency authority can be treated as reversible learned state.

Not demonstrated:

- true interventional urgency credentialing;
- continuous stakes;
- multiple simultaneous fast signals;
- adversarial credential gaming;
- distributed authority agreement;
- real Yggdrasil urgent consequence.

